course: dictionary
lesson: 15665
title: Thoroughfare: a route through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thoroughfare is a road or street that many people and cars use to get from one place to another. Look at the words around it to work out its meaning. «The main thoroughfare through the town was full of buses and shoppers.» Full of buses and shoppers tells you it is a busy road.
explain: Some words on signs can be tricky, but the clues still help. «The sign said No thoroughfare, so we turned back.» Turned back tells you that you were not allowed to go on, so No thoroughfare means you may not go through. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: A thoroughfare can also be a small path or passage, not only a big road. «The narrow thoroughfare between the two shops led to the park.» Narrow and between the shops tell you it is a little way through, like a lane.
fact: A thoroughfare is a main road or street through a town or city, used by lots of traffic and people.
fact: A thoroughfare can also be any route or passage that people go through from one place to another.
fact: «Thoroughfare» is a noun, and its plural is «thoroughfares».
fact: On a sign, «No thoroughfare» means you may not go through. It is often a private road or a dead end.
fact: Useful phrases: a busy thoroughfare, main thoroughfare, no thoroughfare.
exercise: «The busy thoroughfare was full of buses and bikes.» What is a thoroughfare? | A quiet garden with flowers | *A main road with lots of traffic | A kind of tall building | A small pond in a park
exercise: «The sign said No thoroughfare, so we walked the other way.» What does No thoroughfare mean? | Everyone must walk this way | *You may not go through | The shop is open | Please stop and take a photo
exercise: Ali says a thoroughfare is always a huge motorway. What is the better answer? | It must always be a field | It is always a shop | *It can be any road or passage people go through | It must always be a motorway
test: «The narrow thoroughfare led us past the old church to the river.» What does narrow thoroughfare most likely mean? | A deep lake | *A small passage people walk through | A huge stadium | A tall tower
test: Mia says thoroughfare is a type of fish. Why is she wrong? | She is right, it is a fish | Thoroughfare means a fish from the sea | Thoroughfare means a kind of tree | *Thoroughfare means a road or route, not an animal
exam: «The council closed the main thoroughfare for road works, so the buses took a new route.» Why did the buses take a new route? | *Because the busy road was closed | Because the sign said Welcome | Because buses like new routes | Because it was night
